{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "label": "Health checks", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_healthcheckregistry", "label": "HealthCheckRegistry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One registry per ActorSystem that both endpoints aggregate; framework components register into it as they start and your own checks go on the same object. A bare new HealthCheckRegistry is right in a unit test, but in production a second registry is a second notion of ready and only one of them is the one the endpoints read."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_healthchecksof", "label": "healthChecksOf", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reaches the system own registry. The gRPC health service reads the registry you hand it, so passing this one means the two can never disagree about what ready means; a fresh registry there forks them."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_healthcheckresult", "label": "HealthCheckResult", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "name, status and an optional detail; a check may be sync or async, and addLiveness / addReadiness each return an unsubscribe function."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_actor_system_liveness_check", "label": "actor-system liveness check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registered by the registry itself and fails once terminate has completed - the only framework liveness check, because liveness may depend on nothing outside the process."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_cluster_membership_check", "label": "cluster-membership readiness check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Installed by Cluster.join; fails when this node is not up in its own member view."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_cluster_transport_check", "label": "cluster-transport readiness check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately a total-isolation test rather than every-peer-is-reachable: a partial partition leaves the node able to gossip, converge and route, so dropping it from the load balancer would remove capacity from a cluster that is coping. Reachable means an open connection to a peer the failure detector has not written off, and it needs both halves - the canonical partition takes traffic away without producing a FIN or an RST, so sockets stay established while nothing is exchanged. It does not catch the detector own latency, nor a one-way partition in which this node still receives."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_liveness_vs_readiness", "label": "Liveness versus readiness", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Liveness may depend on nothing outside this process: a failing liveness check gets the pod killed, so a check that goes red when a shared database blinks turns one dependency outage into a fleet-wide restart storm, and the restarts cannot fix what broke. Readiness is the right home for exactly what liveness must not touch, because it takes the node out of rotation and leaves it running. A readiness probe that answers 200 while the node cannot reach what it needs is worse than no probe at all."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_leaving_does_not_silence_checks", "label": "Leaving does not silence the checks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "cluster.leave leaves both checks registered and failing, so ready answers 503 for the rest of the process life - which is exactly what drains a pod before it stops. Un-registering would make everything passes and nothing is reporting any more the same answer; a later join retires the old pair and installs its own."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_ishealthy", "label": "isHealthy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The all-pass predicate that the two endpoints and the gRPC health service all apply through the same exported function."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_empty_check_list_is_up", "label": "An empty check list is UP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registering no checks is a statement that nothing gates the probe, so an empty readiness list answers 200 - otherwise every plain cluster-free service behind the management routes would be 503 for its whole life. The rule is only safe because nothing empties the list: a component going quiet reports status false and stays registered."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_no_per_check_timeout", "label": "No built-in per-check timeout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A hung check blocks the whole response, so race a stallable check against your own deadline; without a guard it eventually trips the Kubernetes probe timeout and triggers a restart."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_cluster_ready_flag", "label": "clusterReady flag", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cluster-membership check own result read back out of the aggregate rather than computed separately, so the flag and the check can never contradict each other."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_healthcheckregistry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_healthchecksof", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_healthcheckresult", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_actor_system_liveness_check", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_cluster_membership_check", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_health_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_health_checks_cluster_transport_check", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/health-checks.mdx", 